.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Represents a 3‑component Half16bing‑point vector\&. 

\fBVec3hb\fP is a lightweight numeric type used throughout \fBSystemEx\fP for geometry, math utilities, device operations, and compute kernels\&. It stores two \fBHalf16b\fP values (\fRX\fP and \fRY\fP) in a sequential memory layout, making it compatible with native interop and high‑performance compute backends\&. 

.PP
The struct is annotated with \fBHashAlgorithmAttribute\fP to enable attribute‑driven hashing via HashFactory\&. 
.br
 \fBBernsteinHash\fP is used because it is fast, byte‑linear, and ideal for small fixed‑size numeric types such as vectors\&. 

.PP
\fBVec3hb\fP implements multiple comparison and hashing interfaces: 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
IComparable and IComparable<T> for ordering 
.IP "\(bu" 2
IEquatable<T> for equality checks 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBIHashable<T>\fP for deterministic byte‑level hashing 
.PP
This makes the type suitable for use in dictionaries, sorting, spatial hashing, and compute pipelines\&. 
.PP
